IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mca-court`

-- Magistrates Court Act 2004 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with the seat and the situation as
-- parameters.
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment. Every exported question takes
-- `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"). A question about another role answers `does not arise for you`
-- without reading any other input, so the site's question form never asks those inputs and drops the question.
--
-- ROLES. The baseline (mca-court.l4) was written from the seat of the claimant. What this Act gives a party (who hears
-- the case, where, on what evidence, the s 30 duty to a self-represented party, refused documents, registrars, appeals
-- from them, corrections, the record) it gives every party alike, so the person a claim is brought against asks the
-- same questions and gets the same answers. Someone who is not a party (a witness, or anyone else) meets the Act
-- through contempt (ss 15, 16(4)) and access to the record (s 33(8)):
--   - the claimant: every baseline question;
--   - the other party (the person a claim is brought against): the same questions, asked of both party roles;
--   - a witness or other person who is not a party: contempt, and access to the record.
-- The Court, magistrates, JPs, registrars and the Chief Magistrate are never seats; what they may or must do appears as
-- what it means for the person asking.
--
-- The baseline's `My case` record speaks as the claimant ("my claim", "I am representing myself"). It is the one record
-- both party roles answer, so its @desc here says how its fields read for the other party.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the Graffiti Vandalism Act encoding). Within a role, a question that arises only in a
-- situation takes that situation's fact straight after `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` when it does not
-- hold, without reading anything else. The questions of one situation share one input (same name, type and @desc).
--   - `the case is heard by a bench of two or more JPs` (BOOLEAN): s 7(6). FALSE: does not arise.
--   - `the registry refused to accept a document I lodged` (BOOLEAN): s 17. FALSE: does not arise.
--   - `a registrar has made a decision in my case` (BOOLEAN): s 29, the three appeal questions. FALSE: does not arise.
--   - `the judgment or order in my case has a mistake in it` (BOOLEAN): s 23(1). FALSE: does not arise.
-- All four are taken by both party roles. A question that arises in every situation of its role takes no situation
-- input: the jurisdiction, constitution, place, evidence, s 30, s 28, record and contempt questions.
--
-- The rules are in mca-court.l4. This module calls them and restates none; for the claimant each answer is the baseline
-- export's own answer, wrapped. No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Magistrates Court Act 2004 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am bringing a claim in the Magistrates Court`
    `A claim has been brought against me in the Magistrates Court`
    `I am a witness, or someone else who is not a party to the case`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Days` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `within` HAS `days` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Months` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `imprisonment for` HAS `months` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Whether the Court can hear the claim, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Whether the Court can hear my claim`

DECLARE `Who may hear the case, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Who may hear my case`

DECLARE `What the bench decides, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `What a bench of JPs decides`

DECLARE `My access, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `My access`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

§§ `For a party: the claimant, and the person a claim is brought against`

§§§ `ss 9, 10 -- may the Court hear the claim`

@export May the Magistrates Court hear the claim in my case, and under which law (Magistrates Court Act 2004 (WA) ss 9, 10)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the case` IS A `My case` @desc The case: where the claim's jurisdiction comes from, and the facts of how and where it is heard (for the person a claim is brought against, "my claim" means the claim against you, and "I am representing myself" means you)
GIVETH A `Whether the Court can hear the claim, if it arises`
`May the Magistrates Court hear the claim in my case` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am bringing a claim in the Magistrates Court` THEN `the answer is` (`May the Magistrates Court hear my claim` `the case`)
    WHEN `A claim has been brought against me in the Magistrates Court` THEN `the answer is` (`May the Magistrates Court hear my claim` `the case`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 7, 8 -- who will hear my case, and where`

@export Who may constitute the Court to hear my case (Magistrates Court Act 2004 (WA) s 7(1), (2), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the case` IS A `My case` @desc The case: where the claim's jurisdiction comes from, and the facts of how and where it is heard (for the person a claim is brought against, "my claim" means the claim against you, and "I am representing myself" means you)
GIVETH A `Who may hear the case, if it arises`
`Who may constitute the Court to hear my case` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am bringing a claim in the Magistrates Court` THEN `the answer is` (`Who may constitute the Court for my case` `the case`)
    WHEN `A claim has been brought against me in the Magistrates Court` THEN `the answer is` (`Who may constitute the Court for my case` `the case`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If a bench of JPs hears my case, what is the result of their vote (Magistrates Court Act 2004 (WA) s 7(6))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the case is heard by a bench of two or more JPs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court in your case is made up of two or more Justices of the Peace (s 7(2)(a)), not a magistrate or a single JP
      `JPs for me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the JPs decide in your favour
      `JPs against me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the JPs decide against you
      `every JP was present throughout` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all of the JPs were present at all times while dealing with your case
GIVETH A `What the bench decides, if it arises`
`What is the result of the JPs' vote in my case` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am bringing a claim in the Magistrates Court` THEN
        IF `the case is heard by a bench of two or more JPs`
        THEN `the answer is` (`What does the bench of JPs decide` `JPs for me` `JPs against me` `every JP was present throughout`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `A claim has been brought against me in the Magistrates Court` THEN
        IF `the case is heard by a bench of two or more JPs`
        THEN `the answer is` (`What does the bench of JPs decide` `JPs for me` `JPs against me` `every JP was present throughout`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May the Court sit at that place to deal with my case (Magistrates Court Act 2004 (WA) s 8(1)(c), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the case` IS A `My case` @desc The case: where the claim's jurisdiction comes from, and the facts of how and where it is heard (for the person a claim is brought against, "my claim" means the claim against you, and "I am representing myself" means you)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the Court sit at that place for my case` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am bringing a claim in the Magistrates Court` THEN `yes if` (`May the Court sit there for my case` `the case`)
    WHEN `A claim has been brought against me in the Magistrates Court` THEN `yes if` (`May the Court sit there for my case` `the case`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 14, 30 -- evidence, and representing myself`

@export Do the Supreme Court rules of evidence apply to my case (Magistrates Court Act 2004 (WA) s 14)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the case` IS A `My case` @desc The case: where the claim's jurisdiction comes from, and the facts of how and where it is heard (for the person a claim is brought against, "my claim" means the claim against you, and "I am representing myself" means you)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do the Supreme Court rules of evidence apply in my case` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am bringing a claim in the Magistrates Court` THEN `yes if` (`Do the Supreme Court rules of evidence apply to my case` `the case`)
    WHEN `A claim has been brought against me in the Magistrates Court` THEN `yes if` (`Do the Supreme Court rules of evidence apply to my case` `the case`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 30: "In a case where a party is selfrepresented, the Court must inform the party" -- any party.
@export Must the Court tell me that I have to put my contradicting evidence to the other side's witnesses (Magistrates Court Act 2004 (WA) s 30)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the case` IS A `My case` @desc The case: where the claim's jurisdiction comes from, and the facts of how and where it is heard (for the person a claim is brought against, "my claim" means the claim against you, and "I am representing myself" means you)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the Court explain cross-examination to me as a party` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am bringing a claim in the Magistrates Court` THEN `yes if` (`Must the Court explain cross-examination to me` `the case`)
    WHEN `A claim has been brought against me in the Magistrates Court` THEN `yes if` (`Must the Court explain cross-examination to me` `the case`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 17 -- if the registry refuses my document`

-- s 17(1): "document includes a claim, prosecution notice, application, and affidavit"; (3): "A person affected by such
-- a refusal" -- any party whose document is refused.
@export After the registrar refused a document I lodged as frivolous, vexatious or an abuse of process, may I lodge it (Magistrates Court Act 2004 (WA) s 17)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the registry refused to accept a document I lodged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a registrar refused to accept a document you lodged (a claim, application, affidavit or other document) as frivolous, vexatious or an abuse of the Court's process (s 17(2))
      `a magistrate gave leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a magistrate has given you leave to lodge it
      `I first lodged it within the time limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you first lodged it before any time limit for it ran out
      `the time limit has now expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the time limit for lodging it has run out by now
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I lodge the document the registrar refused` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am bringing a claim in the Magistrates Court` THEN
        IF `the registry refused to accept a document I lodged`
        THEN `yes if` (`May I lodge my refused claim` `a magistrate gave leave` `I first lodged it within the time limit` `the time limit has now expired`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `A claim has been brought against me in the Magistrates Court` THEN
        IF `the registry refused to accept a document I lodged`
        THEN `yes if` (`May I lodge my refused claim` `a magistrate gave leave` `I first lodged it within the time limit` `the time limit has now expired`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 28, 29 -- registrars, and appealing their decisions`

@export May a registrar, rather than a magistrate, take this step in my case (Magistrates Court Act 2004 (WA) s 28(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the step` IS A `A step in my case` @desc The step to be taken in your case
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May a registrar take this step in my case instead of a magistrate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am bringing a claim in the Magistrates Court` THEN `yes if` (`May a registrar take this step in my case` `the step`)
    WHEN `A claim has been brought against me in the Magistrates Court` THEN `yes if` (`May a registrar take this step in my case` `the step`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How many days do I have to appeal a registrar's decision to a magistrate (Magistrates Court Act 2004 (WA) s 29(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a registrar has made a decision in my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a registrar (a court official, not a magistrate) has made a decision in your case that you are dissatisfied with
GIVETH A `Days`
`How many days do I have to appeal the registrar's decision` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am bringing a claim in the Magistrates Court` THEN
        IF `a registrar has made a decision in my case`
        THEN `within` `How many days to appeal a registrar's decision`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `A claim has been brought against me in the Magistrates Court` THEN
        IF `a registrar has made a decision in my case`
        THEN `within` `How many days to appeal a registrar's decision`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I appeal the registrar's decision in my case to a magistrate (Magistrates Court Act 2004 (WA) s 29(1)-(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a registrar has made a decision in my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a registrar (a court official, not a magistrate) has made a decision in your case that you are dissatisfied with
      `it was made under a power delegated by s 28` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the registrar decided in exercise of the Court's jurisdiction or powers delegated under s 28
      `days since the decision` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the date of the registrar's decision you would start the appeal
      `a magistrate extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a magistrate has extended the time for you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I appeal the registrar's decision to a magistrate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am bringing a claim in the Magistrates Court` THEN
        IF `a registrar has made a decision in my case`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can I appeal the registrar's decision` `it was made under a power delegated by s 28` `days since the decision` `a magistrate extended the time`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `A claim has been brought against me in the Magistrates Court` THEN
        IF `a registrar has made a decision in my case`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can I appeal the registrar's decision` `it was made under a power delegated by s 28` `days since the decision` `a magistrate extended the time`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Will my appeal from a registrar be heard afresh (Magistrates Court Act 2004 (WA) s 29(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a registrar has made a decision in my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a registrar (a court official, not a magistrate) has made a decision in your case that you are dissatisfied with
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Will my appeal from the registrar be a new hearing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am bringing a claim in the Magistrates Court` THEN
        IF `a registrar has made a decision in my case`
        THEN `yes if` `Is my appeal from a registrar a new hearing`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `A claim has been brought against me in the Magistrates Court` THEN
        IF `a registrar has made a decision in my case`
        THEN `yes if` `Is my appeal from a registrar a new hearing`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 23 -- mistakes in the judgment`

@export May the Court correct this mistake in the judgment or order in my case (Magistrates Court Act 2004 (WA) s 23(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the judgment or order in my case has a mistake in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you say the judgment or order made in your case is wrong in some way
      `the mistake` IS A `The mistake in my judgment` @desc What is wrong with the judgment or order
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the Court correct this mistake in my judgment or order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am bringing a claim in the Magistrates Court` THEN
        IF `the judgment or order in my case has a mistake in it`
        THEN `yes if` (`May the Court correct my judgment` `the mistake`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `A claim has been brought against me in the Magistrates Court` THEN
        IF `the judgment or order in my case has a mistake in it`
        THEN `yes if` (`May the Court correct my judgment` `the mistake`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 33 -- what I can see of the Court's record of my case`

-- The baseline asks "I am a party"; for both party roles it is TRUE by the role, so it is not asked. Someone who is not
-- a party has a question of their own below.
@export As a party, can I see or get a copy of this from the Court's record of my case (Magistrates Court Act 2004 (WA) s 33(3), (4), (11)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the thing` IS A `What I want from the record` @desc What you want to inspect, copy, see or hear
      `the hearing was electronically recorded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an electronic recording was made of the proceedings
      `a transcript was prepared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a transcript of that recording has been prepared
GIVETH A `My access, if it arises`
`As a party can I get this from the record of my case` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am bringing a claim in the Magistrates Court` THEN `the answer is` (`Can I get this from the record of my case` `the thing` TRUE `the hearing was electronically recorded` `a transcript was prepared`)
    WHEN `A claim has been brought against me in the Magistrates Court` THEN `the answer is` (`Can I get this from the record of my case` `the thing` TRUE `the hearing was electronically recorded` `a transcript was prepared`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For a witness, or someone else who is not a party`

§§§ `s 33(8) -- the record of a case I am not a party to`

-- s 33(8): on an application, the Court "unless it has good reason not to do so, shall give the person leave"; (11)(a):
-- a magistrate's own note need not be made available. The baseline's rule with "I am a party" FALSE.
@export Can I see or get a copy of this from the Court's record of a case I am not a party to (Magistrates Court Act 2004 (WA) s 33(8), (11)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the thing` IS A `What I want from the record` @desc What you want to inspect, copy, see or hear
GIVETH A `My access, if it arises`
`As someone who is not a party can I get this from the record` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a witness, or someone else who is not a party to the case` THEN `the answer is` (`Can I get this from the record of my case` `the thing` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For everyone`

§§§ `s 16(4) -- contempt`

-- s 16(4) reaches "A person guilty of a contempt", whoever they are; s 15(2) makes it a contempt for a summoned witness,
-- or a party required to produce a record, not to do so without reasonable excuse.
@export What is the most I can be fined for a contempt of the Magistrates Court, in dollars (Magistrates Court Act 2004 (WA) s 16(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for a contempt of the Court` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am bringing a claim in the Magistrates Court` THEN amount `What is the most I can be fined for contempt`
    WHEN `A claim has been brought against me in the Magistrates Court` THEN amount `What is the most I can be fined for contempt`
    WHEN `I am a witness, or someone else who is not a party to the case` THEN amount `What is the most I can be fined for contempt`

@export What is the longest I can be imprisoned for a contempt of the Magistrates Court, in months (Magistrates Court Act 2004 (WA) s 16(4); the fine and imprisonment may be imposed together)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Months`
`What is the longest I can be imprisoned for a contempt of the Court` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am bringing a claim in the Magistrates Court` THEN `imprisonment for` `What is the longest I can be imprisoned for contempt in months`
    WHEN `A claim has been brought against me in the Magistrates Court` THEN `imprisonment for` `What is the longest I can be imprisoned for contempt in months`
    WHEN `I am a witness, or someone else who is not a party to the case` THEN `imprisonment for` `What is the longest I can be imprisoned for contempt in months`
